      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "Clinical features (abdominal and paraspinal rigidity, exaggerated lumbar lordosis, limb rigidity), strongly positive GAD65 antibodies, and response to immunomodulation. The authors note the patient partially satisfied Dalakas criteria because of absence of painful spasms and CMUF.",
      "quote": "The presence of abdominal wall rigidity was an important clinical clue that suggested the possibility of SPS despite the presence of LMN features. Serum was strongly positive for glutamic acid decarboxylase (GAD) 65 antibodies... Our patient did not have painful spasms or EMG findings of continuous motor unit firing (CMUF) at rest, hence, partially satisfying the criteria of SPS proposed by Dalakas.",
      "confidence": "high"
